      "text": "The area of the regular hexagon is $\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ units.\nTo find the area of $S$, we need to find the area of the transformation that maps the region $R$ to $S$.\nThe transformation $\\frac{1}{z}$ inverts the points in the complex plane, which maps the outside region to the inside region and vice versa.\nThe transformation $\\frac{1}{z}$ maps a circle of radius $r$ to a circle of radius $\\frac{1}{r}$.\nSo, the area of $S$ is the area of one of the six circles formed by the inverse transformation divided by $6$.\nThe radius of each circle is $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$, so the area of one circle is $\\pi \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^2 = \\frac{\\pi}{3}$.\nTherefore, the area of $S$ is $\\frac{\\pi}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{6} = \\boxed{\\frac{\\pi}{18}}$.\n\nThe answer is: \\frac{\\pi}{18}",
