      "text": "Let $z = x + yi$ be a point in the complex plane where $x$ and $y$ are real numbers. Since $z$ lies outside the unit circle, we have $|z| > 1$. Let $w = \\frac{1}{z}$. Then $|w| = \\frac{1}{|z|} < 1$. So $w$ has magnitude less than 1, and $w^6 = \\frac{1}{z^6} = \\frac{1}{|z|^6} = 1$. Therefore, the image of the part of the real axis inside the unit circle is the unit circle. Thus, the area of $S$ is the area of the unit circle, $2\\pi$. The answer is \\(\\boxed{2\\pi}\\).",
